{"title":"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In equiangular octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59667df6bbc44d3a7606f2796e81571690688fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAROLINE$\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/39761f8b8b4a0d44d040671a35f8a8a607c26cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = RO = LI = NE =$\" width=\"200\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/401c1b663723af1db3654a362d0103b4673230f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AR = OL = IN = EC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"214\" height=\"13\" />. The self-intersecting octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495dba2cf02d4762f1bc8679b455d2c3708b111f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CORNELIA$\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" /> encloses six non-overlapping triangular regions. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the area enclosed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495dba2cf02d4762f1bc8679b455d2c3708b111f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CORNELIA$\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />, that is, the total area of the six triangular regions. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b679c99c2f97b0ed3c2bd7aea0d604cb3b880e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K =$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/52150abefbc7c342c3da94aed4d389997466f2d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df6a591474ffd81edd37d8d9f52f6f476caa531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495dba2cf02d4762f1bc8679b455d2c3708b111f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CORNELIA$\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" /> and introduce some points.\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2018_AIME_II_Problem_4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b6/2018_AIME_II_Problem_4.png/200px-2018_AIME_II_Problem_4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"197\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b6/2018_AIME_II_Problem_4.png/300px-2018_AIME_II_Problem_4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b6/2018_AIME_II_Problem_4.png/400px-2018_AIME_II_Problem_4.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>The diagram is essentially a 3x3 grid where each of the 9 squares making up the grid have a side length of 1.\n</p><p>In order to find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495dba2cf02d4762f1bc8679b455d2c3708b111f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CORNELIA$\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />, we need to find 4 times the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0a21de4d02a9c17e9f716bc93020cb300dc335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup$\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f5196136bbb00c5f2ef9c1fff1a3343e7e30bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACY$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and 2 times the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0a21de4d02a9c17e9f716bc93020cb300dc335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup$\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cbf99af04df72a7735a8693da16efce3a34116d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZW$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Using similar triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0a21de4d02a9c17e9f716bc93020cb300dc335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup$\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f7c3db9abf5aafea382ec06f4fee103d1454ab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ARW$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0a21de4d02a9c17e9f716bc93020cb300dc335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup$\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cbf99af04df72a7735a8693da16efce3a34116d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZW$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />(We look at their heights), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0a21de4d02a9c17e9f716bc93020cb300dc335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup$\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cbf99af04df72a7735a8693da16efce3a34116d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZW$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/37831ad8af616dc1073ddcc422a4d95c5dc8e54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10f7b229549d9afbdef6ae2862bc89bacfe16cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc70a783f789da0c2fd8b8bafa798fe7513503f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = ZQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a56c1a130393e11539eb1f6ddcee8ebe4ce2c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CY$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0a21de4d02a9c17e9f716bc93020cb300dc335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup$\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f5196136bbb00c5f2ef9c1fff1a3343e7e30bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACY$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74ef518e8bd756e2a016ba30b34cfa3a4f9ae156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1fb66751f2ee2626c75303485dba473c39a2f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdot$\" style=\"vertical-align: 3px\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10f7b229549d9afbdef6ae2862bc89bacfe16cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1fb66751f2ee2626c75303485dba473c39a2f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdot$\" style=\"vertical-align: 3px\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1fb66751f2ee2626c75303485dba473c39a2f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdot$\" style=\"vertical-align: 3px\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bf8a8480c95e849be52d2715d00f84d823c9d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/6216c7542b375d61646beb94117c52b065922d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 6 =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f965c65ffafa96e1b4829f464d29824db0a23dc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59667df6bbc44d3a7606f2796e81571690688fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAROLINE$\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" /> is essentially a plus sign with side length 1 with a few diagonals, which motivates us to coordinate bash. We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9bc6c61c1593795727be10710d1e3958fb573f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = (1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5bafdb89b0f11214c7183272c13c2d0d515c6e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = (0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495dba2cf02d4762f1bc8679b455d2c3708b111f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CORNELIA$\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />'s self intersections, we take \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e84c64aff00b4a15af4afe2ac4f5356df0f2e02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CO = y = 2, AI = y = -3x + 6, RN = y = 3x - 3\\]\" width=\"396\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>And plug them in to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/70624e01821eae6259dff5625c3eebf2e7a003be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1 = \\left(\\frac{4}{3}, 2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"103\" height=\"45\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1ba4c023ee85686e3f95ba84eca0681f6bba57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2 = \\left(\\frac{5}{3}, 2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"103\" height=\"45\" /> is the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bddf730477ae3ea7754344d502b5b581f2f9a2da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We also track the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bddf730477ae3ea7754344d502b5b581f2f9a2da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f58de08c35ef86458c10a78fb8a92abf94e521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{3}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"62\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>By vertical symmetry, the other 2 points of intersection should have the same x-coordinates. We can then proceed with Solution 1 to calculate the area of the triangle (compare the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/5677b030478500560c673e756a68a2fe1f5f28ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,R,I,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4dad93e901f5e174ab61b99f61ece541ad3e979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EL$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II\" title=\"2018 AIME II\">2018 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</